"""Practice only. Every option includes its own feedback."""
QUESTIONS=[
 ('Pricing weights','p = 0.625. Which statement follows?', ['The up state is forecast with 62.5% probability','This pricing weight makes the underlying grow at the risk-free rate','The project succeeds technically with probability 62.5%'],1,['A pricing weight is not management’s forecast.','Correct. It supports valuation with risk-free discounting.','Technical success is a separate source of uncertainty.']),
 ('Growth factor','An effective annual rate is 5%, with one-year steps. What is R?', ['0.05','1.05','exp(0.05)'],1,['0.05 is the rate, not the future value of one dollar.','Correct: one dollar becomes 1.05.','That would apply to a continuous annual rate of 5%, a different convention.']),
 ('Growth factor','For continuous r and a half-year step, choose R.', ['exp(r/2)','exp(r)','1+r'],0,['Correct: R = exp(r × dt).','This grows the dollar for a full year.','This is an effective annual convention, not the specified continuous rate.']),
 ('Pricing weights','If d = 0.8, u = 1.2 and R = 1.3, can we use this tree?', ['Yes; set p = 1','No; the no-arbitrage condition fails','Yes; use p = 0.5'],1,['Clipping the probability conceals the invalid inputs.','Correct: R must lie strictly between d and u in these exercises.','A guessed probability does not repair the tree.']),
 ('Backward recursion','Which values belong in the call recursion?', ['Child underlying values','Child option values','The current gate cost twice'],1,['That would value the underlying instead of the call.','Correct. Use the claim’s child values.','Every gate cost is deducted once at its date.']),
 ('Backward recursion','Why divide by R?', ['To bring next-step values back one time increment','To remove volatility','To convert a forecast probability into a pricing probability'],0,['Correct: divide by the growth factor for that step.','Volatility enters the moves and resulting payoffs.','p is derived separately from u, d, and R.']),
 ('Gates','Cgo = 9, K = 10. What are NPVpay and F?', ['−1 and 0','0 and 0','−1 and −1'],0,['Correct: paying loses 1, while declining is worth zero.','Only the option value is clipped at zero.','The right to decline prevents a negative option value.']),
 ('Gates','Cgo = 26.19 and K = 10. Why not compare S = 120 with K?', ['We receive an option worth 26.19, not the operating asset yet','S must always be ignored','The initial cost must first be added to K'],0,['Correct. Identify what the payment buys at that date.','S matters when determining future opportunity values and final exercise.','The initial cost is sunk at this later gate.']),
 ('Gates','At a date with no gate, what do we do?', ['Subtract the last gate cost again','Carry the discounted child option values','Take max(S − final cost, 0)'],1,['Do not charge the same cost twice.','Correct. There is no discretionary payment or exercise at this date.','This incorrectly introduces an extra exercise right.']),
 ('Economic meaning','A green zero at a gate proves that paying has exactly zero NPV.', ['True','False'],1,['It may have negative NPV; the option value is clipped at zero.','Correct. Zero may represent abandonment of a negative-NPV payment.']),
 ('Economic meaning','If we have already paid 5 to reach year 1, should that 5 enter the year-1 decision?', ['Yes, subtract it again','No; compare only future value and the new cost'],1,['That would double-count a sunk cost.','Correct. The starting decision includes 5, but the later decision does not.']),
 ('Economic meaning','Can a profitable terminal node still be inaccessible?', ['No, a recombining tree restores access','Yes, if this path encountered an earlier abandonment'],1,['Recombination applies to underlying values, not to extinguished rights.','Correct. Decisions at nodes are conditional on still holding the opportunity.']),
 ('Construction','When n changes in a CRR tree with fixed maturity, what changes?', ['Only the number of nodes','dt, u, d, R, and p','The final investment cost automatically'],1,['Keeping old moves would change the model rather than refine it.','Correct: recalibrate every step-dependent input.','The contract’s strike does not change with the numerical grid.']),
 ('Construction','Does adding observation steps automatically add payment gates?', ['Yes','No'],1,['Gate dates are contractual or managerial opportunities, not a numerical artifact.','Correct. Keep the gate schedule separate from the computational grid.']),
 ('Construction','Will every extra CRR step move the call price closer to Black–Scholes?', ['Yes','No; convergence may oscillate'],1,['Step-by-step improvement is not guaranteed.','Correct. One to four steps are too coarse to establish a convergence trend.']),
 ('Economic meaning','An opportunity is worth 3.68 before an initial cost of 5. What should we report?', ['Starting NPV −1.32; option to start 0; do not begin','Starting NPV 0; begin','Starting NPV 3.68; begin'],0,['Correct. Report the signed investment NPV separately from the option to decline.','Zero is the value of declining, not the signed NPV of paying.','3.68 excludes the initial cost.']),
]
